        "root_concepts": "[riemann, hypothesis]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Riemann Hypothesis",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ZEROS:\n  Trivial zeros: s = -2, -4, -6, ...  [from the functional equation]\n  Non-trivial zeros: s = σ + it with 0 ≤ σ ≤ 1 (known region)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:number-theory:08-riemann-hypothesis, git-history:number-theory:08-riemann-hypothesis]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md",
        "concepts": "[riemann, hypothesis]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:riemann-hypothesis",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[riemann, hypothesis]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Riemann Hypothesis",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RIEMANN HYPOTHESIS:\n  Every non-trivial zero s = σ + it satisfies σ = 1/2.\n  Equivalently: all non-trivial zeros lie on the line {1/2 + it : t ∈ R}."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "08-RIEMANN-HYPOTHESIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
